  "reason": "The records repeatedly establish mechanical/high-energy ball milling of equiatomic elemental HEA powders under argon followed by short vacuum SPS consolidation, including milling durations near 5–6 h and systematic evidence that milling time controls refinement, homogenization, phase formation, contamination, and hardness. They also collectively identify nanocrystalline grain-boundary strengthening, solid-solution hardening, lattice distortion, and Ti atomic-size and melting-point effects as relevant mechanisms. R7 is especially close compositionally, addressing Ti effects in an AlCoCrFeNiTi-type alloy, while R1, R2, R14, R18, and R19 supply the processing template. Although the exact CoCrFeNiTi temperature window, FCC/BCC fractions, and quantitative properties are not disclosed, an expert could plausibly combine these teachings to propose the later intervention and its principal strengthening mechanism."
